//
// Phase E4 runlist-mode gate: the D2 layer at the fine-grained point of the
// execution-strategy taxonomy.
//
// Same golden model and same per-boundary comparisons as the block, coarse and
// offload gates, behind a different execution boundary: thirteen
// single-operator entries over two runlists -- q/k/v projections; host torch
// blocked attention (the implementation offload shares, unchanged); then
// output_proj, residual add, LayerNorm, gamma multiply, up_proj, GeLU,
// down_proj, residual add, LayerNorm, gamma multiply -- each runlist forced to
// one submission. Intermediates inside a runlist stay device-resident. No GEMM
// ELF executes twice: the four projections are one module compiled to four
// artifacts, because re-execution in one hw_context corrupts INSIDE a single
// runlist exactly as it does across submissions (pattern/runlist/README.md has
// the measurement).
//
// Two recipes in one file, deliberately: they share a working directory and
// therefore the ELF cache, so the injected run reuses the ten ELFs the clean
// run compiled -- compilation depends on the shape, not the data.
//
// NPU serialization lives one layer down, not in the recipes below: device
// access is locked on /tmp/npu.lock inside KernelCache, the same inode
// lit.cfg.py's NPU substitution takes. Taking the outer /tmp/mlir-air-npu.lock
// here would DEADLOCK against the gate command that already holds it -- BSD
// flock(2) treats a second open() of the same file as a foreign lock.
//
// Editing this header: lit scans the WHOLE file for its directives, so naming
// one in prose -- even inside a comment -- registers as a second directive and
// leaves the test UNRESOLVED. Describe them, never spell them out.
//
// REQUIRES: ryzen_ai_npu2, peano
//
// RUN: mkdir -p test_npu2_runlist_peano
// RUN: cd test_npu2_runlist_peano
// RUN: make -f %S/Makefile clean
// RUN: make -f %S/Makefile check-runlist PEANO_INSTALL_DIR=%PEANO_INSTALL_DIR | FileCheck %s
//
// The configuration first -- the forced gate configuration, each GEMM resolved
// through the registry, and the mode's own statement of its decomposition and
// its host attention boundary. A registry change that moved a method fails
// here with its cause on screen.
// CHECK: runlist 4096x768 ffn 3072 12h x 64 (encoder_bert, non-causal, 13 fine-grained entries over 2 runlists, attention in host torch)
// CHECK: proj 4096x768x768 drain (registry), up 4096x768x3072 drain (registry), down 4096x3072x768 fused-cast (registry)
// CHECK: attention host torch fp32, query block 4096 x1 block(s)
//
// Every boundary, in execution order, each with zero mismatching elements.
// Named individually rather than counted, so a stage list that dropped or
// repeated an entry fails here -- the driver requires at least eight DISTINCT
// names, and this is where the suite enforces the same thing.
// CHECK: [stage] q {{.*}} mismatch       0
// CHECK: [stage] k {{.*}} mismatch       0
// CHECK: [stage] v {{.*}} mismatch       0
// CHECK: [stage] attn_context {{.*}} mismatch       0
// CHECK: [stage] attn_out {{.*}} mismatch       0
// CHECK: [stage] hidden {{.*}} mismatch       0
// CHECK: [stage] ffn_up {{.*}} mismatch       0
// CHECK: [stage] ffn_gelu {{.*}} mismatch       0
// CHECK: [stage] ffn_out {{.*}} mismatch       0
// CHECK: [stage] output {{.*}} mismatch       0
// CHECK: [runlist] stages: 10/10 clean
//
// The mode's own instrumentation: one DispatchVector row per runlist. Two --
// a wrapper that split a runlist per operator (offload's shape), or stopped
// recording per-sequence rows, fails here before the driver's totals
// comparison sees it.
// CHECK: [runlist] recorded 2 dispatch vectors
//
// The vectors' CONTENTS, not only their count: the six driver-summed totals.
// Two submissions over thirteen entries is the mode's decomposition made
// checkable. Air is 11 (one launch per drain ELF -- q/k/v in runlist 1, then
// o/add/ln/mul/up/gelu in runlist 2 -- plus two for the fused-cast down
// projection, each ELF counted once per sequence it appears in); herd counts
// accumulate per entry; sync is 21 (runlist 1: x + three weights up, q/k/v
// back; runlist 2: ctx, x, five statics and the down projection's f32 scratch
// up, six declared boundaries back); and the bytes are those twenty-one
// transfers exactly. The totals line prints only after every row passes the
// as_row() schema validation, so a malformed row aborts the run and a run
// whose totals drift fails right here. NOTE the 13 entries land BELOW
// coarse's 131 -- the honest fine-grained count, measured, with the finding
// recorded in pattern/runlist/README.md.
// CHECK: [runlist] dispatch totals: submissions 2 entries 13 air 11 herd 26 sync 21 bytes 152567808
//
// Then the layer output itself over all 4096 x 768 elements, and the label
// naming the MODE's operator.
// CHECK: PASS!
// CHECK: [opcheck] runlist [4096x768_encoder_bert]: PASS
//
// THE NEGATIVE CONTROL. Identical reasoning to the offload gate's --
// ln1_weight, chosen by measurement, perturbed AFTER the golden model was
// computed -- plus the stake every Phase E mode carries: the dispatch vectors
// must be recorded on the injected path too, because the driver requires the
// fault artifact's summed totals to EQUAL the clean run's.
//
// RUN: make -f %S/Makefile check-runlist-fault PEANO_INSTALL_DIR=%PEANO_INSTALL_DIR | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=FAULT
//
// The injected element first, so an injection that silently perturbed nothing
// is visible here rather than read backwards from the verdict. Index 5 is
// ln1_weight in RUNLIST_INPUT_NAMES -- the q/k/v weights are separate in this
// mode, so the index matches offload's and differs from the block's.
// FAULT: [fault-inject] input 5 at (0,)
//
// Nothing upstream of the first gamma multiply reads ln1_weight, so the whole
// attention half must still be exact while `hidden` and everything after it
// moves -- which is what says the stage comparisons are reading THIS run's
// buffers rather than replaying the clean run's. In this mode the perturbed
// weight reaches the device as a re-materialized static broadcast, so a
// content-keyed cache that failed to re-upload it would show up here as a
// clean `hidden`.
// FAULT: [stage] q {{.*}} mismatch       0
// FAULT: [stage] attn_out {{.*}} mismatch       0
// FAULT: [stage] hidden {{.*}} mismatch {{[1-9][0-9]*}}
// FAULT: [runlist] stages: 5/10 clean
//
// The vectors, still recorded under injection -- and totaling EXACTLY what
// the clean run totals: the six literals below are the same six the clean
// half pins above, which is the suite's own statement of the equality the
// driver re-derives from the two artifacts.
// FAULT: [runlist] recorded 2 dispatch vectors
// FAULT: [runlist] dispatch totals: submissions 2 entries 13 air 11 herd 26 sync 21 bytes 152567808
//
// And the verdict in the three forms opcheck.py reports it: the comparison's
// own, the control's reading of it, and the exit-status summary.
// FAULT: [opcheck] runlist [4096x768_encoder_bert]: FAIL
// FAULT: [opcheck] runlist [4096x768_encoder_bert]: fault-inject input -> FAIL (as required)
// FAULT: NEGATIVE CONTROL: PASS
